Subject: [PATCH] spmi: msm: encode one-byte transfers with byte count zero

Both msm_spmi_read() and msm_spmi_write() transfer exactly one byte. The
PMIC arbiter command byte-count field stores length minus one, so encoding
1 asks for two bytes. In particular, a one-byte write must not modify the
following PMIC register using the unused upper write-data byte.

Primary reference: Linux v6.12, drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c#L386-L421
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c#L464-L500
The read/write command constructors both use bc = len - 1, and the v1/v2
formatters encode bc & 7 in command bits 2:0:
https://github.com/torvalds/linux/blob/v6.12/drivers/spmi/spmi-pmic-arb.c#L1427-L1435

diff --git a/drivers/spmi/spmi-msm.c b/drivers/spmi/spmi-msm.c
--- a/drivers/spmi/spmi-msm.c
+++ b/drivers/spmi/spmi-msm.c
@@ -95,12 +95,14 @@
 
 static u32 pmic_arb_fmt_cmd_v1(u8 opc, u8 sid, u8 pid, u8 off)
 {
-	return (opc << 27) | (sid << 20) | (pid << 12) | (off << 4) | 1;
+	/* This API transfers one byte; hardware encodes byte count minus one. */
+	return (opc << 27) | (sid << 20) | (pid << 12) | (off << 4);
 }
 
 static u32 pmic_arb_fmt_cmd_v2(u8 opc, u8 off)
 {
-	return (opc << 27) | (off << 4) | 1;
+	/* This API transfers one byte; hardware encodes byte count minus one. */
+	return (opc << 27) | (off << 4);
 }
 
 static int msm_spmi_write(struct udevice *dev, int usid, int pid, int off,
